and the `# 29. Optional: external live-Dokploy smoke tests` known-good fixture to `# 30. Optional…`) in the SAME edit. The renumber cost is bounded — only static tests that pin step headers in the affected range need updates — but a missed update fails the analyser self-check, NOT silently. Forward-applicable to every future required-step insertion: grep all `# N. Optional` and `# N. Required` literals in `internal/release/verification_suite_*_static_test.go` for the renumbered range and update each in the same commit; the AGENTS.md subsection for the inserting story documents the renumber as the shared cost. (2) `PURE PROJECTION HELPERS (NO LIVE INFRASTRUCTURE) STILL KEEP THE CANONICAL PAIR SHAPE` — the release package's `ArchiveExt`/`BinaryName`/`ArchiveName`/`ChecksumsName` are pure functions today, so the contention-burst member of the canonical pair would seem redundant. But the burst is the load-bearing stability check the gate's wire contract requires AND keeping the pair shape consistent across every BE-0379..BE-0401 gate makes the static analyser's canonical-funcs matcher reusable and the operator-facing AGENTS.md narrative consistent. Forward-applicable: every future verification-suite gate (pure-function or stateful) keeps the closed-set-coverage + per-decision-stability pair shape so the `-run TestX` filter binds to a two-function fixture the static gate can name, even when the burst's race tripwire is the only load-bearing reason for the second function to exist.

